<Layout title="Session 119 — Tales of the Radiant Citadel" description="Gordian joined the party in the Ludendorff library. He projected a Bluetspur brain's memories into his homunculus's mist, and proved himself by nearly sett">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <a href="/studio" class="text-sm text-earth hover:text-ink transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">&larr; Studio</a>

    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black leading-tight mb-2">
      Session 119
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-earth mb-1">Tales of the Radiant Citadel &middot; November 3, 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mb-8">Return to the Radiant Citadel (post-Bluetspur)</p>

    <div class="prose-section text-ink-light leading-relaxed mb-12 space-y-4">
      <p>
        Gordian joined the party in the Ludendorff library. He projected a Bluetspur brain's memories into his homunculus's mist, and proved himself by nearly setting the library on fire. The party named him <strong>G-0</strong> and gave him a first mission: find his own voice. The party went back to a Radiant Citadel that is &quot;holding its breath.&quot; The ghoul army is camped beneath the crystal, Commissar Lee is evacuating the city behind illusions, and Edzinka is quietly bankrolling the defense. At the Bastion the party met two teenage hill giants, Gemnar traded his dragon trophies for a flying mount, Haru set up a hatchery for the silver dragon eggs, and Islana's research finally explained Kiet's ring. Kenazaro split his soul in two, and the other half is a statue in Io'nido.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Highlights</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-12 list-disc list-inside">
      <li><strong class="text-ink">A New Day</strong> — Sam started a daily ritual for Gordian: <em>&quot;Gordian, you have a thing that you get to do at the beginning of every day, which is roll dice to see what your experimental elixirs are.&quot;</em> Erik pitched it as the standing pre-session routine: Sam says &quot;it's a new day,&quot; Erik rolls elixirs and sets the day's build. Sam: <em>&quot;Today is a new day for you. It is your first day, in fact.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Clever, Clever, Clever</strong> — Gordian studied the Bluetspur lab gear. Sam: <em>&quot;This seems to be a whole apparatus for taking other people's memories and learning things from them.&quot;</em> Erik: <em>&quot;I'll kind of pause for a second as if to indicate the end of a washing machine cycle,&quot;</em> then played Haru's voice back: <em>&quot;clever, clever, clever.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">G-0</strong> — Asked who he is, Gordian points to the serial number on his head. Sam: <em>&quot;Is that an O or G-0? We'll call him G-0 for now.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Willing to Burn Down a Library</strong> — Kiet asks if he can sword fight. Gordian juggles caltrops like a circus act. Sam: <em>&quot;Your worth to the party might be demonstrated with a spell rather than juggling.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Elixirs, Day One</strong> — Rolled <strong>2, 3, 3, 4</strong>: Swiftness, Resilience ×2, Boldness. Sam's ruling: <strong>&quot;You do know what they are. It would be madness otherwise if you just had to drink it on faith.&quot;</strong></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Radiant Citadel Is Closed</strong> — Crossing Ludendorff, the party sees the Concord Jewels arriving full and leaving empty, a one-way flow out of the Citadel. Shieldbearers now run every crossing.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Commissar Lee, Ten Years Older</strong> — Shieldbearer HQ is packed with more Shieldbearers than the party has ever seen, most of them learning firearms for the first time.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Thick and Thack</strong> — Following Virgil's standing order for more muscle, Steps Without Looking hired <strong>two teenage hill giants</strong>. <em>&quot;If they were any bigger, they probably wouldn't fit in.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Barred for Life</strong> — Kiet introduces G-0 to Ben at the casino. Ben: <em>&quot;You brought us another clanker? We already have two.&quot;</em> Kiet: <em>&quot;Make sure he doesn't do any gambling here. He might walk away too much of a winner.&quot;</em> Erik: <strong>&quot;He just introduced me and barred me for life.&quot;</strong> <em>&quot;Welcome to the casino. This is your first and last time here.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Creepy Wing</strong> — Sigmar spots Gordian at once: <strong>&quot;Interesting work. You look like a custom job. Are you one of a kind, or are you from a line that I'm unfamiliar with?&quot;</strong> Gordian plays Sigmar's own words back to him: <em>&quot;One of a kind.&quot;</em> Nobody mentions the voice box, so Sigmar goes back to his office.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Flying Giant on a Giant Fly</strong> — Gemnar finds a fellow giant-kin running a market stall. To Gemnar that makes him <em>&quot;obviously a coward because he's a shopkeeper rather than a barbarian.&quot;</em> The pitch: <em>&quot;Fine wares from the giant lands.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Hatchery</strong> — In the temple, Haru brings out the two silver dragon eggs Bahamut purified and gave him, and asks for help: <em>&quot;Between the two of you and the three of us, holy and knowledge and love and lore beasts, I feel like we can turn this temple into not just a sacred space but a hatchery.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Kenazaro, at Last</strong> — Islana's research on the wizard <strong>Kenazaro</strong>: he was <em>&quot;a sellsword of spells, a wizard for hire,&quot;</em> who fought at <strong>Atash's</strong> side when Pazuzu was first imprisoned. The ring came from Atash's hoard. <em>&quot;So, yes, there's a logic here.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Team Meeting</strong> — <strong>Edzinka:</strong> Kiet raised her first: she's getting too powerful, and Edzinka controlling the Shieldbearers <em>&quot;does not feel like a good situation.&quot;</em> Table: <em>&quot;Maybe now is finally the time to knock over the soda machine and kill her.&quot;</em> The pushback: <em>&quot;Guys, she's supplying weapons that we need. Of all the things to kill her for, this is not the time.&quot;</em> Table: <em>&quot;Billionaire tax Toven over here.&quot;</em> Sam on campaign tradition: <em>&quot;One of which is we start killing Edzinka and then don't.&quot;</em> For the record: Edid has tried to kill her at least once, Kiet at least once, Boris saved her once or twice, and Toven saved her last time. Verdict: not now.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Art</h2>
    <div class="space-y-10">
      {images.map((img) => (
        <figure>
          <img
            src={img.src}
            alt={img.title}
            class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-lg"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">{img.title}</span>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mt-1">{img.caption}</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-cream-dark mt-16 pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold mb-3">Party</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Gordian (G-0)</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Erik)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Kiet</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Jonas)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Virgil Gemnar</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Kyle)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Toven</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Max)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Haru</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Hunter)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">DM</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Sam)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
